From 8ff4d0eaa98f97460762ede092eb3804e9593bda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: y-o-o-z <136268860+y-o-o-z@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:09:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] local: Source Sans 3 and Source Code Pro instead of Geist

The shellter theme now uses Adobe's Source family: Source Sans 3 for text
and interface, Source Code Pro for time, the nick column, the nick list and
code. Both SIL OFL 1.1, hosted with the theme: one variable file per subset
(weights 200-900), latin + latin-ext for Polish letters, italics only
downloaded when italic text appears. Text is 15px instead of the base
sheet's 14px, as Source Sans 3 has a smaller x-height. The nick list is
monospaced: in a proportional face "I" and "l" are nearly the same
(124IA4IU3), in IRC nicks they are different characters, and Source Code
Pro tells 0 from O. No ligatures where IRC text is shown in the mono face.
The fonts used from the first frame are preloaded with the same URL as in
the stylesheet.

Fonts: @fontsource-variable/source-sans-3 5.3.0,
@fontsource-variable/source-code-pro 5.3.0; licenses in
client/themes/shellter/fonts/OFL-*.txt.
